    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but small actions dont actually change anything though. like what's the point in planting a tree or recycling when the feedback loops are already set in motion? it feels like we're just rearranging deck chairs on the titanic. it's hard to find motivation for a future that i don't even believe exists anymore. i just feel so exhausted by the whole thing.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The feeling that your efforts are meaningless is a very real and valid exhaustion, but it doesn't negate the power of your own experience. While massive systems are complex, those small actions are what build the momentum for change, even if the change feels slow. For now, perhaps the point isn't fixing the whole Titanic, but finding a small, sustainable act of peace or purpose *for yourself* in the midst of the storm.",
      "source": "target",
